{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For it is a festival of YHWH to us.</b> This is the festival of Shavuot, the day of the giving of the Torah, for He had already said to him (Exodus 3:12): ״בהוציאך את העם ממצרים תעבדון את האלהים על ההר הזה״ — 'when you bring the people out of Egypt you shall serve Elohim on this mountain.' And one should not interpret it as the festival of Pesach, for they performed the Pesach in Egypt; nor is it possible to interpret it as Sukkot, for it has no mention on the mountain of Elohim. Rather, it is the festival of Shavuot, which falls in the month of Sivan, as it is written (Exodus 19:1): ״בחדש השלישי לצאת בני ישראל מארץ מצרים ביום הזה באו מדבר סיני״ — 'in the third month after the children of Israel came out of the land of Egypt, on this day they came to the wilderness of Sinai.' And this day was Rosh Chodesh Sivan, and HaShem kept them waiting there for two days, and on the morrow, on the sixth day, the Torah was given."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:28.484286448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}